Fixed copy of the release audit (to_publish/tools/verify_no_leakage.py, sha256 in logs/audit_script_sha256.txt),
for review round 2 (R2-027, D4, R2-102). The original is not edited. Run from a directory in the release layout
(stage_release/, built by stage_release_layout.py + stage_fixed_extra.py). Every check prints what it tests.

Changes against the release script:
  B3/B4  every one of the 20,000 rows, not 500 spread-out rows.
  C3     the scored sets are read from the v1.44 per-shot files (campaign_v144/final/{axi,live,inloop}), not the v1.40/
         v1.41 ones; C5 (new) re-derives the v1.44 ledger fidelities from those files with rows 1000:1600 removed and
         compares them with campaign_v144/final/analysis/v144_stats.json, i.e. it checks that the reported numbers are
         the masked sets.
  D      D2  the FIR-path file (0528_X_train_0_770_loopback_calibrated.npy, NN_axi) on EVERY row, not 200;
         D2b (new) the boxcar-path file NN_live trains on (0528_X_train_box_calibrated.npy + _rows.npy), every row,
             against kb*MA_M(x)[n-s]+cb from calibration/box_domain_map.json, with the builder's own filter code;
         D3  (rewritten) searches each mapped training file for any row equal, within a tolerance, to a TEST row
             pushed through the same map (or to a raw test row): mapped rows and test rows are compared in the same
             dtype and domain, so the check can fail. The release D3 compared blake2b hashes of float32 mapped rows
             with hashes of float64 raw test rows (always disjoint) on the first 20,000 rows only.
         --d3-file / --d3-selftest run D3 alone on a given (e.g. deliberately corrupted) file.
  F      F2 (new) the boxcar-path map equals the label-free refit from its recorded capture and differs from the
         per-class fit (which needs labels).
  G      G5 reads the v1.44 NN_live runs (each board: run 1 + run 2 = every row once).
  R2-102 every input is checked up front; a check whose inputs are missing is recorded BLOCKED, not a traceback.

